OL,3,AChancellor rejects calls to raise
OL,4,ACapital Gains Tax in Budget
OL,5,
OL,6,FChancellor of the Exchequer John Healey
OL,7,Fhas dismissed calls from some Labour
OL,8,FMPs to increase Capital Gains Tax (CGT)
OL,9,Fwhen he hands down his first Budget.
OL,11,FCabinet ministers Wes Streeting and
OL,12,FLouise Haigh both previously voiced
OL,13,Fsupport for raising CGT before Andy
OL,14,FBurnham became prime minister in July.
OL,16,FAhead of next week's Budget, Healey
OL,17,Fruled out lifting CGT - which is
OL,18,Fimposed on the profit people make when
OL,19,Fthey sell an asset that has increased
OL,20,Fin value, such as shares in a company
OL,21,For properties which are not primary
OL,22,Fresidences.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
